IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV, "Offences": sections 106 and 107.
-- Who commits an offence under Part IV and what the court may impose; the overlap with administrative penalties; the
-- liability of a corporation's officers, directors and agents.
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- A punishment is stated as the range the court may impose (a minimum and a maximum), never as the sentence: the court decides
-- the sentence. "Summary conviction" procedure is the Criminal Code's (not deposited) and is not restated.
-- Imprisonment is counted in months (six months is 6).

§ `Section 106(1) to (3) - contraventions`

-- src:1733 | 106 (1) Every employer who contravenes subsection 82(1) or 86(2) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(1) (src:1733)
GIVEN `contravenes subsection 82(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contravenes subsection 86(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` IF
        `contravenes subsection 82(1)`
    OR  `contravenes subsection 86(2)`

-- (a) a fine of not more than $5,000; or (b) both the fine and imprisonment for not more than six months.
-- src:1733 | 106 (1) Every employer who contravenes subsection 82(1) or 86(2) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to
-- src:1734 | (a) a fine of not more than $5,000; or
-- src:1735 | (b) both the fine and imprisonment for a term of not more than six months.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(1) (src:1733-1735)
GIVEN `the fine` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(1) the punishment is within what the subsection allows on summary conviction` IF
        `the fine` AT MOST 5_000
    AND `the term of imprisonment in months` AT MOST 6

-- src:1737 | (2) Every person who contravenes section 87 or 88 is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(2) (src:1737)
GIVEN `contravenes section 87` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contravenes section 88` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` IF
        `contravenes section 87`
    OR  `contravenes section 88`

-- Subsection (3): a fine "of not less than $25 a day for each day of default, but not more than $1,000 in all". For a default of
-- more than 40 days the daily minimum (25 x days) would exceed the $1,000 ceiling; the ceiling is read as prevailing, so the
-- least fine is the smaller of 25 x days and 1,000 (fork F-ei3-24).
-- src:1739 | (3) Every person who contravenes regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 a day for each day of default, but not more than $1,000 in all.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(3) (src:1739)
GIVEN `contravenes regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(3) the person is guilty of an offence` IF
    `contravenes regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b)`

-- src:1739 | (3) Every person who contravenes regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 a day for each day of default, but not more than $1,000 in all.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(3) (src:1739)
GIVEN `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 106(3) the least fine` IS
    IF (25 TIMES `the number of days of default`) LESS THAN 1_000
    THEN 25 TIMES `the number of days of default`
    ELSE 1_000

-- src:1739 | (3) Every person who contravenes regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 a day for each day of default, but not more than $1,000 in all.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(3) (src:1739)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 106(3) the most the fine can be in all` MEANS 1_000

§ `Section 106(4) to (6) - false statements, evasion, punishment`

-- Subsection (4): every person is guilty of an offence who (a) makes, or participates in, assents to or acquiesces in the making of,
-- false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or Part
-- VII.1 or the regulations; (b) to evade payment of a premium, destroys, alters, mutilates, secretes or otherwise disposes of an
-- employer's records or books of account; (c) makes false or deceptive entries in them, omits to enter a material particular, or
-- assents to or acquiesces in either; (d) wilfully evades or attempts to evade compliance with the Act or payment of premiums;
-- (e) conspires with any person to commit an offence described in (a) to (d).
-- src:1741 | (4) Every person is guilty of an offence who
-- src:1742 | (a) makes, or participates in, assents to or acquiesces in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or Part VII.1 or the regulations;
-- src:1743 | (b) to evade payment of a premium imposed by this Act, destroys, alters, mutilates, secretes or otherwise disposes of the records or books of account of an employer;
-- src:1744 | (c) makes false or deceptive entries in records or books of account of an employer, omits to enter a material particular in the records or books of account or assents to or acquiesces in the making or omission of the entries;
-- src:1745 | (d) wilfully, in any manner, evades or attempts to evade compliance with this Act or payment of premiums imposed by this Act; or
-- src:1746 | (e) conspires with any person to commit an offence described in paragraphs (a) to (d).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(4) (src:1741-1746)
GIVEN `makes, or participates in, assents to or acquiesces in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or Part VII.1 or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to evade payment of a premium imposed by this Act, destroys, alters, mutilates, secretes or otherwise disposes of the records or books of account of an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `makes false or deceptive entries in records or books of account of an employer, omits to enter a material particular in them, or assents to or acquiesces in the making or omission of the entries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wilfully, in any manner, evades or attempts to evade compliance with this Act or payment of premiums imposed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conspires with any person to commit an offence described in paragraphs (a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(4) the person is guilty of an offence` IF
        `makes, or participates in, assents to or acquiesces in the making of, false or deceptive statements in a return, certificate, statement or answer filed or made as required by or under this Part or Part VII.1 or the regulations`
    OR  `to evade payment of a premium imposed by this Act, destroys, alters, mutilates, secretes or otherwise disposes of the records or books of account of an employer`
    OR  `makes false or deceptive entries in records or books of account of an employer, omits to enter a material particular in them, or assents to or acquiesces in the making or omission of the entries`
    OR  `wilfully, in any manner, evades or attempts to evade compliance with this Act or payment of premiums imposed by this Act`
    OR  `conspires with any person to commit an offence described in paragraphs (a) to (d)`

-- Subsection (5): "in addition to any penalty otherwise provided", on summary conviction (a) a fine of not less than $25 and not more
-- than $5,000, plus, in an appropriate case, not more than double the premium that should have been shown to be payable or that was
-- sought to be evaded; or (b) both the fine and imprisonment for not more than six months.
-- src:1748 | (5) In addition to any penalty otherwise provided, the person is liable on summary conviction to
-- src:1749 | (a) a fine of not less than $25 and not more than $5,000 plus, in an appropriate case, not more than double the amount of the premium that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded; or
-- src:1750 | (b) both the fine and imprisonment for a term of not more than six months.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(5) (src:1748-1750)
GIVEN `the fine, not counting any addition by reference to the premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the addition by reference to the premium, in an appropriate case` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(5) the punishment is within what the subsection allows on summary conviction` IF
        `the fine, not counting any addition by reference to the premium` AT LEAST 25
    AND `the fine, not counting any addition by reference to the premium` AT MOST 5_000
    AND `the addition by reference to the premium, in an appropriate case` AT LEAST 0
    AND `the addition by reference to the premium, in an appropriate case` AT MOST (2 TIMES `the premium that should have been shown to be payable or that was sought to be evaded`)
    AND `the term of imprisonment in months` AT MOST 6

-- Subsection (6): a person convicted under this Part for contravening s 82(1) or regulations under 108(1)(a) or (b) is not liable to
-- pay a penalty under s 82 or a regulation under s 108 for the same contravention UNLESS assessed for it, or it was demanded of them,
-- before the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made. If not convicted the subsection is silent.
-- src:1752 | (6) If a person has been convicted under this Part for contravening subsection 82(1) or regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b), the person is not liable to pay a penalty imposed under section 82 or under any regulation made under section 108 for the same contravention unless the person was assessed for that penalty or it was demanded from them before the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 106(6) (src:1752)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted under this Part for contravening subsection 82(1) or regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was assessed for the penalty, or it was demanded from them, before the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 106(6) the person is liable to pay the penalty for the same contravention` IS
    IF `the person has been convicted under this Part for contravening subsection 82(1) or regulations made under paragraph 108(1)(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST `the person was assessed for the penalty, or it was demanded from them, before the information or complaint giving rise to the conviction was laid or made`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 107 - officers, directors and agents of corporations`

-- src:1754 | 107 If a corporation commits an offence under this Part, any officer, director or agent of the corporation who directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on conviction to the punishment provided for the offence, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 107 (src:1754)
GIVEN `a corporation commits an offence under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer, director or agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 107 the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment` IF
        `a corporation commits an offence under this Part`
    AND `the person is an officer, director or agent of the corporation`
    AND `the person directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the commission of the offence`
